A K-9 team working the USBP Immigration Checkpoint near Alamogordo, NM, alerted to a pickup truck attempting to pass through. After a thorough inspection, agents discovered four bundles of cocaine weighing a total of 9.9 pounds concealed inside a hidden compartment.
The driver was arrested and now faces federal drug charges.

